WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.400
Now, your family owned [shrimp drying] platforms.

2
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:07.260
I think a hurricane changed your mind about owning . . .

3
00:00:07.260 --> 00:00:07.880
Yeah.

4
00:00:07.880 --> 00:00:16.200
In 1926 a hurricane came right through Terrebonne Parish and blew away a lot of the platforms.

5
00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:23.940
And my grandfather and his partner had a boat and they sent the boat to go get the people on one particular platform,

6
00:00:23.940 --> 00:00:27.420
I think it was out by the Seabreeze [Pass].

7
00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:36.740
And the boat broke down and they had nine people left out of the platform, including a little boy that had gone fishing with his daddy.

8
00:00:36.740 --> 00:00:42.540
And they got caught on that platform, and nine people drowned.

9
00:00:42.540 --> 00:00:45.400
My grandfather and his partner decided that, at that that time,

10
00:00:45.400 --> 00:00:50.050
they were going to try to get rid of those platforms because they didn't want to have that responsibility on them.

11
00:00:50.050 --> 00:00:55.940
If people wanted to dry the shrimp they could do it on their own you know, and we would buy it from them.

12
00:00:55.940 --> 00:01:00.620
And they parked the boats and stuff behind the shop and we still have . . . In fact,

13
00:01:00.620 --> 00:01:05.060
one of the masts off of one of the boats is supporting the building in the back, back there.

14
00:01:05.060 --> 00:01:06.816
If you want to go walk back there and look [laughing].
